  {"comment":"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. Construction geometry on the edges and vertices of sheet bodies (mitcad#1537), placements within 1e-6 mm (relative tolerance 5e-9 on coordinates below 200 mm). Rules t=2, r=3, K=0.3, the reference side the front. Three sheets: a 40 x 20 x 2 plate converted to a sheet of one panel (F2.b0, its edges lines); a 40 x 30 x 20 block at x = 100 converted to a U channel of its bottom and end faces (F4.b0); a 60 x 20 Face at y = 50..70 folded 90 degrees up at x = 0 (F7.b0). The channel's and the folded sheet's straight edges are B-spline curves (the sheet's paired rails), which the datums take as lines. The fold's bend allowance is (pi/2)(r + K t) = 1.8 pi, half of it c = 0.9 pi: the upright's front lies at x = 5 - c, its top at z = 35 - c, its back at x = 3 - c."},
